From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] lab(#53 w1 challenger): no repaint inset on coverage sides at
 the image edge

The detail layer repainted whenever cropInside(crop, coverage, 12% inset)
failed. Coverage is clamped to the image, so below ~1.32x zoom, or with
the crop on an image edge, that test can never pass: every render()
repainted the full detail canvas with identical coverage and tiles (lab
trace: 22 back-to-back ~100 ms repaints at rest, zoom 1.19).

cropEscapes() keeps the inset on interior sides and drops it on sides
already at the image boundary. Experimental candidate for Quackles Lab;
not for promotion without phone evidence.

